    "title": "Rep. Thomas Massie Introduces Legislation to Withdraw the U.S. from NATO",
    "text": "• Rep. Thomas Massie (R-Ky.) introduced the 'NATO Act' (H.R. 6508) to withdraw the U.S. from NATO.\n• The bill would direct the president to notify allies of U.S. withdrawal under Article 13 of the North Atlantic Treaty.\n• The bill would bar the use of U.S. taxpayer money for NATO's common budgets.\n• Rep. Anna Paulina Luna (R-Fla.) is co-sponsoring the bill.\n• Sen. Mike Lee (R-Utah) has filed companion legislation in the Senate.\n• A 2023 law requires approval from two-thirds of the Senate or an act of Congress for the U.S. to leave NATO.\n• A 2024 AP-NORC poll found 61% of Americans believe NATO membership is good for the U.S.\n• A 2025 Pew Research report indicated six in ten adults have a favorable view of the alliance.\n• According to Reuters reports from 2024, Donald Trump has pressured NATO allies on defense spending.\n• NATO leaders adopted a new pledge to spend 5% of GDP on defense by 2035.",
